<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kumasi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kumasi is a city in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a> and was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti Empire</a>. It was the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asantehene">Asantehene</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-stool">Golden Stool</a>, and the centre of the empire's government and trade. The city was occupied by British forces during the Anglo-Ashanti wars, and its capture marked the empire's loss of independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kumasi.jpg" alt="Kumasi" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Maven Egote · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kronum_Kumasi_2018-11-08_(130246).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
